      "content": "Here's a summary that you can use as a starting point: \n\nA 64-year-old male with a history of hypertension and Type 2 Diabetes presented with sudden onset left-sided weakness and facial drooping. His neurological examination revealed slurred speech and decreased sensation on the left side, with palpable weakness in the left upper extremity. The CT scan showed ischemic changes in the territory of the Middle Cerebral Artery (MCA), although details were limited by the patient's movement during the scan. His vitals and labs support the possibility of an evolving stroke, but not definitively rule out a transient ischemic attack or transient metabolic imbalance.",
